\code{UMFPACKFactorization}, \code{PureUMFPACKFactorization},
\code{SparspakFactorization}, \code{CHOLMODFactorization},
\code{SparseColumnPivotedQRFactorization}, \code{CliqueTreesFactorization},
\code{ParUFactorization}, \code{CKTSOFactorization}, \code{HSLMA57Factorization},
\code{HSLMA97Factorization}, \code{MUMPSFactorization}, \code{MKLPardisoFactorize},
\code{MKLPardisoIterate}, \code{PanuaPardisoFactorize}, \code{PanuaPardisoIterate},
\code{PardisoJL}, \code{SuperLUDISTFactorization}, \code{SupernodalLUFactorization},
\code{STRUMPACKFactorization}, \code{SLATEFactorization} and \code{ElementalJL} select a
library or a device in Julia; R has one BLAS and LAPACK, so they compute
the same LU, QR or Cholesky factorization through it (dense).

Krylov methods (implemented in R; \code{abstol}, \code{reltol}, \code{maxiters},
\code{restart} and the preconditioners \code{Pl}, \code{Pr} are options of \code{solve()}):
\code{KrylovJL_GMRES()}, \code{KrylovJL_FGMRES()} (restarted GMRES with right
preconditioning), \code{KrylovJL_CG()} (conjugate gradients), \code{KrylovJL_MINRES()}
and \code{KrylovJL_MINARES()} (symmetric indefinite), \code{KrylovJL_BICGSTAB()},
\code{KrylovJL_LSMR()} (least squares, by CGLS) and \code{KrylovJL_CRAIGMR()}
